  "documented_exceptions": [
    "Non-Dairy in 2.3.51/2.3.52 official product name does NOT imply no milk allergen: sodium caseinate derived from milk is expressly permitted. The actual product formula must be checked.",
    "The powder standard 2.3.63 also permits sodium caseinate; the printed bulk-density source has a stray terminal ']' after 0.45, so this audit reads 0.30–0.45 g/ml only as a conditional FSSR source interval, and original Gazette must govern if any conflict.",
    "Maltodextrin and coconut water also expressly allowed where described; unrelated automatic dairy analogue categorisation is prohibited.",
    "Milk allergen declaration may be triggered by added sodium caseinate; do not claim vegan or milk-free for a formulation actually containing this milk-derived ingredient.",
    "Where manufacturer claims vegan, verify all ingredients, processing aids and actual vegan logo endorsement under current applicable regulations; vegan is not inferred from the 'Non-Dairy' standard title.",
    "Liquid coconut milk and cream have named LIGHT/NORMAL and CREAM/CONCENTRATE styles, which cannot be selected solely by marketing wording; inspect actual solids, fat, moisture, SNF and pH.",
    "90% minimum fill condition in the printed standards is specific to hermetically sealed containers, not an arbitrary universal container-fill declaration.",
    "Powder fat must be on DRY basis, while liquid fat/solids are measured on w/w (as sold) basis; conversion method and laboratory results required.",
    "Do not inherit cow milk aflatoxin M1, coconut oil metal/pesticide article, coconut water commodity article or raw coconut crop MRL simply because source coconut or word milk appears.",
    "Full original Gazette/current amendments, micro Appendix B, additives, packaging/claim/labeling, test reports and any valid finished-product contaminant matrix remain open."
  ],
